# Named Tables: Multiple Tables and Cross-References
# Two tables in one document with calculations that reference both.

<!-- table: hardware (item, unit_cost, qty) -->
| Item     | Unit Cost | Qty |
|----------|-----------|-----|
| Server   | $4500     | 12  |
| Switch   | $800      | 6   |
| Storage  | $12000    | 4   |

---

hw_line = hardware.unit_cost * hardware.qty
hw_total = sum(hw_line)

---

<!-- table: labor (role, monthly, months) -->
| Role       | Monthly Rate | Duration |
|------------|--------------|----------|
| Architect  | $18000       | 6        |
| Engineer   | $14000       | 12       |

---

labor_line = labor.monthly * labor.months
labor_total = sum(labor_line)
project_total = hw_total + labor_total

---

## Table without directive is inert

Regular markdown tables are untouched — no directive means no extraction.

| This | Table |
|------|-------|
| is   | inert |
| just | prose |
